meta {
  name: Review Row
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/carrier-reconciliation/runs/{{reconRunId}}/rows/{{reconRowId}}/review
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{reconToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "resolved",
    "resolution": "service_set_up",
    "note": "Allstate 1-800 policy; set up for service by Bruno"
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("records the decision and who made it", function () {
    const review = res.getBody().review;
    expect(review.status).to.equal("resolved");
    expect(review.resolution).to.equal("service_set_up");
    expect(review.reviewedBy.name).to.be.a("string");
    expect(review.reviewedAt).to.be.a("string");
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /carrier-reconciliation/runs/:id/rows/:rowId/review — decide a row

  - **Module:** `carrier_reconciliation`
  - **Permission:** `carrier_reconciliation:write`

  ## Body
  - `status` — `open` | `resolved` | `dismissed`
  - `resolution` — required with `resolved`: `entered_in_app`,
    `number_corrected`, `credit_corrected`, `premium_corrected`,
    `carrier_figure_wrong`, `service_set_up`, `timing`, `not_ours`,
    `duplicate`, `other`. The page offers the ones that fit the row's tabs:
    - Missing from app — `entered_in_app`, `number_corrected`, `not_ours`, `other`
    - Not in Dash — `number_corrected`, `timing`, `not_ours`, `duplicate`, `other`
    - 1-800 review — `service_set_up`, `not_ours`, `other`
    - Premium differs — `premium_corrected`, `carrier_figure_wrong`, `other`
    - Producer mismatch — `credit_corrected`, `other`

    `confirmed_1800` is retired (a 1-800 policy is now set up for service):
    a review can no longer set it, a row decided with it still reads back with
    its label, and a re-upload reopens that row instead of carrying it.

    `sold_recorded`, `cancel_rewrite_recorded` and `other_recorded` are
    refused too (`400`): only an assignee's finished outcome writes them
    (PAC-173 PR 4), and a row decided that way reads back with them.
  - `note` — optional, ≤ 2000 characters; omitted keeps the current note

  Reopening (`open`) clears the resolution and the reviewer. A decision on a
  superseded run's row is carried to the new run only if the row still has
  the same match and issues.

  ## The assignee's outcome (PAC-173 PR 4)
  - **Reopening** clears the outcome, finished or not: the row asks again,
    and the decision an outcome wrote is the one being taken back. A deal it
    booked stays booked.
  - **Deciding by hand** (`resolved` / `dismissed`) while an outcome is
    still under way clears it, so a sale booked on it later changes nothing
    here.
  - A **finished** outcome is otherwise left as the record of what was done,
    whatever the row is now decided as.

  ## Errors
  - `400` — validation (an outcome resolution included), or `resolved`
    without a `resolution`
  - `404` — no such run or row in the agency
  - `409` — the assignee recorded something on the row at the same moment;
    reload and decide again
}
